# Whether an interval x of the round-up interval is a subset of y: x empty, or -yn <= -xn and xu <=
# yu, the first written xn <= yn; the default interval_subset_1 on the meanings. Exact, in every
# rounding mode (docs/developer/design/upward.md, "Predicates and comparisons"). Requires the
# rounding mode upward set by kairn::upward::Scope and the options of docs/concepts/upward.md (GCC
# and Clang -frounding-math, MSVC /fp:strict).
kernel:        upward_subset_1
rounding:      upward
input:         pair stored x = xu xn
input:         pair stored y = yu yn
output:        mask m
requires:      upward xu xn
requires:      upward yu yn
ensures:       certain m subset x y x=xu,xn y=yu,yn exact
min_precision: 1
source:        the lanes compared, and a test of emptiness (the listing of the round-up interval)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_only:     yes
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the result is a mask, which has no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; certain states what comes out for every canonical operand

ex = unord(xu, xu)
a = le(xn, yn)
b = le(xu, yu)
c = and(a, b)
m = or(ex, c)
